{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Survey: the pytest-only repo-invariant gate class is ~70 modules, not three.\n\nMethod: enumerate every `scripts/*.py` invocation in the Makefile `lint` target (23 gate\nscripts + ruff/zizmor/actionlint), then sweep tests/unit, tests/scripts and tests/interfaces\nfor modules whose assertions are about the committed tree rather than runtime behaviour,\nexcluding those that merely unit-test a script `make lint` already runs.\n\nFamilies found beyond the three named on this ticket:\n- CI-config / workflow parity: test_ci_workflow_parity, test_verify_gate_parity,\n  test_ci_actionlint_scope, test_typecheck_scope, test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring,\n  test_probe_wired_into_ci, test_ci_main_push_policy, test_ci_tickets_push_policy,\n  test_workflow_names, test_gate_step_tree_skew, test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew,\n  test_release_workflow_pins, test_worktree_python_pin, test_git_version_floor (~20).\n- Ratchets/baselines: test_complexity_baseline(+_lock_47e9), test_module_size_contract,\n  test_mypy_ratchet, test_ruff_ratchet, test_config_surface_golden,\n  test_packaging_dependencies.\n- Whole-tree AST/policy scans: test_core_optionality, test_deprecation_registry,\n  test_tests_import_convention, test_scripts_import_convention,\n  test_repo_root_install_agnostic, test_nested_pytest_uniqueness,\n  test_collection_isolation_guard, test_error_handling_convention,\n  test_alarm_actions_terraform and others.\n- Generated-artifact / docs drift: the five test_gen_*.py check-mode tests,\n  test_check_docs_index, test_generated_surface_markers, test_env_registry_helper_coverage,\n  test_client_template_sync, test_skill_shared_sync, plus tests/interfaces/contracts/*\n  (public types, schema coverage, exit-code doc conformance, tombstone registry).\n\nConsequence for the fix: a curated node list or a hand-applied pytest marker would be a\nsecond list to keep in sync with this population — the same drift defect one level up, and\nthe class this repo already builds derive-and-diff gates (check_deploy_manifest.py) to stop.\nSo the resolution is the complete-by-construction one: `make verify` = lint + typecheck +\n`make test`, where `make test` already carries exactly CI's DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS\n(`not integration and not external`). Nothing to enumerate, nothing to drift.\n\nMeasured on this host (worktree venv, macOS): make lint 27s, make typecheck 10s, and the\nthree named gate tests together 67s serial / 11.6s under `-n 4 --dist worksteal` — which is\nwhy `make test` gains `-n auto --dist worksteal` (CI already runs the suite under xdist)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788513618747208001,"uuid":"2e2de733-18ac-4942-ad9e-5ec5c3387b93"}